# Docker matches these against the whole relative path, so a pattern without a separator only
# ever matches at the root (F-713). `**/` is what makes one match at any depth — and depth is
# not hypothetical here: AGENTS.md documents a sibling git worktree at .worktrees/main, a
# complete second checkout carrying its own node_modules, .next and .env.local. Root-anchored
# patterns let all of that into the build context and into the `builder` layer, where a leaked
# intermediate layer or `docker history` exposes credentials the final image never COPYs.
#
# Nothing in the build reads a .env file: `next build` and `prisma generate` take DATABASE_URL
# from the Dockerfile's placeholder ENV, and no source file reads .env.example. So there is no
# `!**/.env.example` re-include — env files are excluded outright.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.git
**/.github
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/generated
**/coverage
**/.turbo
**/.vercel
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.DS_Store

# Second checkouts and agent scratch space, each with their own installs and env files.
.worktrees
.claude
.cursor

# Not needed by `prisma generate` or `next build`.
tests
# The spec files stay out, but `next build` type-checks every file in the context and
# two of them import from e2e/support (`playwright.config.ts` → ./e2e/support/paths,
# `scripts/seed-e2e-account.ts` → ../e2e/support/seed-account) — with the whole tree
# excluded, the production build failed on TS2307 (deploy 2026-08-29). The helpers are
# a few small files importing only lib/, generated/ and @playwright/test, all present
# in the builder.
e2e
!e2e/support/**
playwright-report
test-results
examples
audit
agent-transcripts
.data
*.tar.gz
e2b-template-*
*.tmp
*.temp
*.md
!README.md
!docs/**
